            <ArticleTitle>[Radiolucent and opaque lesions on a panoramic radiograph; a cyst or not?]</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>481-483</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5177/ntvt.2017.10.17123</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the context of pain diagnostics, several lesions, partially radiolucent and partially opaque, were identified by chance in the mandible and maxilla. On the basis of the characteristic x-ray image, it was assumed to be cemento-osseous dysplasia. At an early stage, this cannot easily be distinguished from apical periodontitis. An incorrect diagnosis could lead to needless endodontic treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
